      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/06-herrings-relationship/anchoviella-alleni-2/",
      "html": "<p>Anchoviella alleni is one of the very few representatives of the anchovy family (Engraulididae) that lives exclusively in freshwater. The species attains a maximum length of about 10 cm.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "distribution",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/06-herrings-relationship/anchoviella-alleni-2/",
      "html": "<p>The fish were imported from Peru.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "dimorphism",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/06-herrings-relationship/anchoviella-alleni-2/",
      "html": "<p>The supposed males are more slender, slightly larger and the swim bladder has a different shape, compared with the supposed females.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "notes",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/06-herrings-relationship/anchoviella-alleni-2/",
      "html": "<p>The specimens received were about half of the maximum size, around 5 cm.</p>"
    }
  ],
